{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.not_of_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.not_of_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthday.lean#L175-L200","doc":"**Inhabitation depends on the data** — the property the old schema lacked\nentirely.\n\nThe quadratic trajectory is **refuted**: `0` is algebraic, and `n²` outruns\nevery `C · log n + C`. Under the previous shape no choice of anything could\nfail, so a wrong trajectory had nothing to fail against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.nonempty_of_const_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.nonempty_of_const_zero","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthday.lean#L165-L173","doc":"**Not over-corrected**: the identically-zero trajectory satisfies the class,\nso its openness is not an artefact of emptiness. Degenerate data deliberately —\nthe content is only that a witness exists at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.transcendental_of_not_logarithmic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.transcendental_of_not_logarithmic","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthday.lean#L143-L158","doc":"**A super-logarithmic trajectory forces transcendence** — the block's title,\nderived from part 1 alone.\n\nIf `α`'s trajectory outruns every logarithmic bound, `α` cannot be algebraic.\nThis is the separation the block claims, and it needs only the unhedged half of\nthe conjecture; the hedged converse (part 2) is not required and is not\nassumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.algebraic_logarithmic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.algebraic_logarithmic","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthday.lean#L120-L120","doc":"**Part 1 — algebraic rigidity.** For algebraic `α` the trajectory is\n`O(log n)`. The constant is existential and `α`-dependent because the\nblock ties it to the degree of `α`; a single global constant would be a\nstronger claim than the block makes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday.mk","kind":"ctor","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthday.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthday","kind":"class","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthday.lean#L104-L123","doc":"**Birthday-trajectory discrimination**: algebraic numbers have logarithmic\nbirthday trajectories.\n\nThe unhedged half of\n[`conj:diophantine-birthday`](../../../appendix-surreals-archimedean/diophantine-birthday.md).\n\n`trajectory α n` is the block's `b_α(n)` — the minimum birthday among best\nrational approximations to `α` with denominator at most `n`. It is the caller's\ndata; this library constructs no such function.\n\nAn instance **is** the conjecture, for that trajectory. None is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:diophantine-birthday","label":"conj:diophantine-birthday","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/diophantine-birthday.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}